  idleMessage: "ATLAS V 401  \u2022  INSIGHT MARS LANDER\nVandenberg Air Force Base,
    Space Launch Complex 3E  \u2022  May 5, 2018, 4:05 a.m. PDT\n\nPress the red
    LAUNCH button to start the countdown."
  ignitionMessage: RD-180 main engine start!
  liftoffMessage: 'LIFTOFF!

    Atlas V lifts off carrying the InSight lander to
    Mars.'
  pitchMessage: 'Heading south over the Pacific Ocean.

    The first launch to another
    planet from the West Coast.'
  stagingMessage: 'Climbing into the fog.

    On launch morning, thick fog hid the
    rocket from most people watching.'
  cruiseMessage: 'InSight is on its way to Mars!

    Landing: Elysium Planitia,
    November 26, 2018.


    (Real launch timeline sped up.)'
  briefingNarrationText: NASA's InSight lander launched aboard an Atlas V 401 from
    Vandenberg Air Force Base in California on May 5, 2018. The launch window opened
    at 4:05 a.m. Pacific Daylight Time. InSight was sent to study the deep interior
    of Mars. Press the red launch button when you are ready. This is a shortened
    educational reenactment.
